  "body": "## Issue\nDirect-PR: a label requested by the operator (2026-11-07), defined where labels live.\nClaim: ext/francoisgn-suborch-1\n\n## What and why\n- The operator wants statistics on what device testing finds.\n- `.github/labels.yml` gains `beta-test finding`, with colour `f9a825`.\n- AGENTS.md §7 defines it next to the other credit label.\n- The label already exists on the repository: it was created when it was applied to the issues of 2026-11-07 (#566, #568–#570, #572, #579, #580, #582, #584, #592–#596, #425, #427, #512). The sync workflow sets its colour and description once it runs.\n\n## How it was verified\nmarkdownlint is clean on AGENTS.md. The YAML line follows the format of the other entries.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Docs only\n- [x] No secrets\n- [ ] Author model: Opus 5.5 / Reviewer: the operator or any other model\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ4JPCeiaUyzcb2HYv)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added the **beta-test finding** label for issues reported during pre-beta or beta testing on a device. Its description clarifies which findings qualify, and the label can remain on issues for statistics.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
